  <h1>BRIDGES — Shipment Exception Control Tower</h1>
  <div class="doc-subtitle">Complete Application Flow, Role Governance & Page Architecture Guide</div>

  <table style="width: 100%; background: #f8fafc; margin-bottom: 24pt;">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 25%;"><strong>System Version:</strong> BRIDGES v2.6.4</td>
      <td style="width: 25%;"><strong>Total Roles:</strong> 7 Personas Gated</td>
      <td style="width: 25%;"><strong>Total Views:</strong> 62 Functional Views</td>
      <td style="width: 25%;"><strong>Local URL:</strong> http://localhost:8080</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h2>1. System Architecture & Operational Lifecycle</h2>
  <p>
    BRIDGES is an enterprise-grade multimodal logistics Control Tower and shipment exception mitigation platform. It links real-time IoT and GPS telemetry to operational decision-makers across the logistics chain.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 25%;">Phase</th>
        <th style="width: 40%;">Operational Function</th>
        <th style="width: 35%;">Responsible Personas</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>1. Ingestion & Detection</strong></td>
        <td>GPS positions and IoT sensor streams (temperature, humidity, shock) are ingested in real-time. Automated SLA rules flag deviations.</td>
        <td>IoT Telematics &bull; System Store</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>2. Diagnostic & Triage</strong></td>
        <td>Incidents are prioritized by severity (Critical, High, Medium) with SLA countdown clocks. Root causes are analyzed in Investigation Workspaces.</td>
        <td>Control Tower Analyst</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>3. Planning & Intercept</strong></td>
        <td>Dispatchers evaluate detour corridors, calculate transit overhead, and issue tenders (Expedite, Carrier Swap, Freight Splitting).</td>
        <td>Dispatcher / Transport Planner</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>4. Fleet Execution</strong></td>
        <td>Carriers review and accept tenders, assign backup vehicles and drivers, perform pre-trip inspections, and confirm gate departure.</td>
        <td>Carrier Operations User (`CAR-01`)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>5. Hub Cross-Docking</strong></td>
        <td>Warehouse floor supervisors allocate dock doors, verify cold-chain stability with physical probes, and sign off security gate handovers.</td>
        <td>Warehouse Supervisor (`WH-DAL-01`)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>6. Stakeholder Advisory</strong></td>
        <td>Customer care specialists review approved arrival windows and use AI Copilots to draft clear, non-blaming proactive delay notifications.</td>
        <td>Customer Service</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>7. Shipper Delivery & ePOD</strong></td>
        <td>Customers track cargo through arrival. Drivers capture digital signatures and photo evidence for electronic Proof of Delivery.</td>
        <td>Customer / Shipper &bull; Carrier Driver</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

