  <h2>4. End-to-End Walkthrough Example: Cold-Chain Incident Lifecycle</h2>

  <div class="step-box critical">
    <div class="step-title">Step 1: IoT Detection & Automated Alerting (IoT Telematics &bull; Store)</div>
    <p>
      Shipment <strong>BRG-2843</strong> (BioPharma Critical Vaccine Consignment) is in transit from Dallas to Mountain Knot via refrigerated unit <code>RT-04</code>. The IoT sensor detects a temperature spike to <strong>-14.2°C</strong>, breaching the mandatory contract limit of <strong>-20.0°C</strong>. An automated Critical Exception is raised.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="step-box critical">
    <div class="step-title">Step 2: Control Tower Triage & Forensics (Analyst Sarah Lin)</div>
    <p>
      Sarah Lin receives the Critical Alert on the <strong>Exception Queue</strong> (<code>#/analyst_queue</code>). In the <strong>Investigation Workspace</strong> (<code>#/analyst_investigation</code>), she inspects the telematics telemetry curve and detects a secondary refrigeration compressor stall. She launches a <strong>War Room</strong> session (<code>#/analyst_war_room</code>) and flags the incident for immediate cross-dock intercept.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="step-box warning">
    <div class="step-title">Step 3: Route Re-planning & Carrier Recovery Tender (Dispatcher Elena Rostova)</div>
    <p>
      Elena Rostova opens the <strong>Planning & Routing Workspace</strong> (<code>#/dispatcher_planning</code>). She identifies an emergency rendezvous point at the Dallas Central Hub (`WH-DAL-01`), minimizing the added transit deviation to 1 hour 45 minutes. In <strong>Carrier Recovery Operations</strong> (<code>#/dispatcher_recoveries</code>), she issues Expedite Tender <code>REC-2005</code> to partner <code>CAR-01</code> (Bridges Global Logistics).
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="step-box warning">
    <div class="step-title">Step 4: Carrier Tender Acceptance & Driver Dispatch (Carrier Marcus Vance)</div>
    <p>
      Marcus Vance reviews the notification in <strong>Recovery Requests</strong> (<code>#/carrier_requests</code>) and accepts tender <code>REC-2005</code>. In <strong>Dispatch Execution</strong> (<code>#/carrier_execution</code>), he assigns relief refrigerated truck <code>BG-12</code> and driver <code>Norman Reedus</code>, completing the pre-trip checklist and dispatching the vehicle to the Dallas hub.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="step-box">
    <div class="step-title">Step 5: Warehouse Hub Intake & Quality Inspection (Warehouse Carlos Mendoza)</div>
    <p>
      At Dallas Hub (`WH-DAL-01`), Carlos Mendoza sees the emergency arrival on his <strong>Warehouse Dashboard</strong> (<code>#/warehouse_dashboard</code>). In <strong>Dock Scheduling</strong> (<code>#/warehouse_docks</code>), he assigns Bay 2. In <strong>Shipment Readiness</strong> (<code>#/warehouse_readiness</code>), his team performs a manual temperature probe check, verifies thermal stability, transfers the vaccine pallets to truck <code>BG-12</code>, and logs driver departure in <strong>Carrier Handover</strong> (<code>#/warehouse_handover</code>).
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="step-box">
    <div class="step-title">Step 6: Customer Care Advisory via AI Copilot (Customer Service Clara Hughes)</div>
    <p>
      Clara Hughes spots the revised arrival window in her <strong>Customer Service Queue</strong> (<code>#/cs_queue</code>). In the <strong>CS AI Copilot</strong> (<code>#/cs_ai_assistant</code>), she generates a customer-safe message explaining a "routine equipment safety swap with cold-chain stability verified" confirming a revised delivery window of 2:30 PM. She sends the advisory via <strong>Compose Communication</strong> (<code>#/cs_compose</code>).
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="step-box success">
    <div class="step-title">Step 7: Customer Self-Service Tracking & Final Delivery (Customer Sarah Jenkins &bull; Driver)</div>
    <p>
      Sarah Jenkins opens her <strong>Customer Home</strong> (<code>#/customer_home</code>), reviews the notification, and monitors the final leg on <strong>Track Shipment</strong> (<code>#/customer_track</code>). Upon truck arrival at Mountain Knot, driver Norman Reedus captures her digital signature and photo in <strong>Delivery Confirmation</strong> (<code>#/carrier_delivery</code>). The electronic Proof of Delivery (ePOD) is instantly archived in both portals.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="step-box success">
    <div class="step-title">Step 8: Governance & Permanent Audit Record (Administrator Bima Ary)</div>
    <p>
      Administrator Bima Ary reviews the completed incident in <strong>Exception History</strong> (<code>#/exceptions</code>). Carrier Bridges Global Logistics receives full SLA credit in <strong>Carrier Management</strong> (<code>#/carriers</code>) for meeting the expedited turnaround time. The complete sequence is permanently written to the immutable <strong>System Audit Log</strong> (<code>#/audit</code>).
    </p>
  </div>

</body>
</html>
